  "sites": [
    {
      "id": "1.3:1",
      "quote": "The examples skip some required parameters for reasons of simplicity.",
      "disposition": "excluded",
      "excluded-kind": "not-a-requirement",
      "reason": "Descriptive: says the examples in the document omit some required parameters; it states nothing an implementation does"
    },
    {
      "id": "2:1",
      "quote": "The client must present all necessary parameters for the server to execute the command on the selected router.",
      "disposition": "excluded",
      "excluded-kind": "binds-another-role",
      "reason": "Binds the looking-glass API client, the HTTP caller that sends the request ('The client must present all necessary parameters'). Ze is the server; the client is outside Ze, and Ze holds no looking-glass API client code"
    },
    {
      "id": "2:2",
      "quote": "The path component of the resource URI must use the prefix of \".well- known/looking-glass\" (see Section 5.1) to stay namespace neutral.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "2:3",
      "quote": "The client must not be able to execute random commands on the targeting router.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "2:4",
      "quote": "There must not be any direct communication between the client and the router.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2-3"
    },
    {
      "id": "2.2:1",
      "quote": "The server must ignore its value.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2.2-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3:1",
      "quote": "The response text must comply with the JSON syntax specification JSend, which is briefly explained in Appendix A.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2.3-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3:2",
      "quote": "Consequently, every response must contain a \"status\" field of either \"success\", \"fail\", or \"error\" as explained in the following sections.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2.3-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3.1:1",
      "quote": "A successful response must set the \"status\" field to \"success\".",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2.3.1-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3.1:2",
      "quote": "It must also contain a \"data\" object including the following information:",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2.3.1-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3.1:3",
      "quote": "This information must be present.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2.3.1-3"
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3.1:4",
      "quote": "This information must be present. router Name of the router that executed the command.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2.3.1-4"
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3.1:5",
      "quote": "Adding more information to the response is permitted and must be placed inside the \"data\" object.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2.3.1-5"
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3.2:1",
      "quote": "The response message must set the \"status\" field to \"fail\" and must contain the \"data\" object with command-specific content listed in Section 2.3.1.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2.3.2-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3.3:1",
      "quote": "The response message must set the \"status\" field to \"error\" and must contain the \"message\" key, which keeps a meaningful message, explaining what went wrong.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2.3.3-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3.3:2",
      "quote": "The response may contain the \"data\" key with required values listed in Section 2.3.1.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2.3.3-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "3.3:1",
      "quote": "The following organizational commands must be included in the implementation.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-3.3-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "3.3.2:1",
      "quote": "The response must contain the router's hostname and router index.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-3.3.2-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "6:1",
      "quote": "The use of HTTPS is required to ensure a high level of security, privacy, and confidentiality during transit.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-6-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "A:1",
      "quote": "A basic JSend-compliant response must contain a \"status\" key and should contain \"data\", \"message\", and \"code\" keys dependent on the status value.",
      "disposition": "excluded",
      "excluded-kind": "duplicate-of",
      "reason": "Restates the status-key obligation of Section 2.3 for JSend in general; the 'should contain' part is advisory and keyed to the status value, which Sections 2.3.1 to 2.3.3 state per status",
      "mapped-to": "RFC8522-2.3-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "A:2",
      "quote": "The following table lists the required and optional keys.",
      "disposition": "excluded",
      "excluded-kind": "not-a-requirement",
      "reason": "Descriptive: introduces Table 1; 'required' names a column of the table"
    },
    {
      "id": "A:3",
      "quote": "+---------+-----------------+---------------+ | Type | Required keys | Optional keys | +---------+-----------------+---------------+ | success | status, data | | | fail | status, data | | | error | status, message | code, data | +---------+-----------------+---------------+",
      "disposition": "excluded",
      "excluded-kind": "not-a-requirement",
      "reason": "Table 1 of JSend keys; its Required column restates the per-status obligations of Sections 2.3.1, 2.3.2 and 2.3.3, which are mapped there"
    }
  ]
}
